; Regression: page inference rule 1 — a no-sigil construction of a heap-backed
; type (StringBuilder, whose init takes a page) defaults to the function's
; local page, exactly as an explicit `$` would. Before page inference,
; `StringBuilder()` left the ctor with an Unspecified lifetime, so
; emit_constructor_call had no page to allocate on → garbage page → SIGSEGV.
; First step toward abolishing the `$`/`#` page sigils: the programmer writes
; `StringBuilder()` and the compiler picks the page. Self-hosted-only (frozen
; stage-0 has no page inference).
; Expected: PASS

package scaly 0.1.0

use scaly.containers.StringBuilder

function build_len() returns int
{
    let sb StringBuilder()
    sb.append "hello"
    sb.append " world"
    sb.get_length() as int
}

let n build_len()
if n = 11
    print("PASS")
else
    print("FAIL")
